# Server security

- Do not weaken **[server/server.js](server/server.js)** without explicit approval: CORS allowlist (`CLIENT_URL` + dev origins), **Helmet** (as configured), **`/api` rate limiting** via [server/src/middleware/rateLimiter.js](server/src/middleware/rateLimiter.js), JSON body size limit.
- **Secrets:** API keys (e.g. Gemini) and `JWT_SECRET` only via `process.env`; see [server/src/configs/gemini.js](server/src/configs/gemini.js) pattern — never hardcode keys.
- **Uploads:** follow existing **multer** setup under [server/src/middleware/multer.js](server/src/middleware/multer.js) and `uploads/`; validate required files like blog flows.
- **Mongo:** avoid passing unsanitized user input as raw query operators; the project depends on `express-mongo-sanitize` — do not suggest removing security-related dependencies to “simplify” unless the user explicitly asks.
